# Multi-theme

## Defaults

- Default theme: **`light`** (`DEFAULT_THEME` in `~/lib/constants`).
- Dark mode must stay **architecturally ready** even when the UI still ships light-first.

## Token rules

- Colors go through **semantic tokens** in `src/styles/tokens.css` (`--background`, `--foreground`, `--primary`, …).
- Light values live on `:root`; dark overrides live under `.dark`.
- Components must use semantic Tailwind colors (`bg-background`, `text-foreground`, `border-border`, `bg-primary`, …), not raw hex/oklch in JSX.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
className="bg-white text-black dark:bg-zinc-950"

// ✅ GOOD
className="bg-background text-foreground"
```

## Coding for both themes

- Prefer tokens that already flip under `.dark`; add `dark:` only for intentional theme-specific tweaks.
- When adding a new semantic color, define **both** light (`:root`) and dark (`.dark`) values in `tokens.css`.
- Do not assume dark is unavailable — layouts, contrast, borders, and shadows must remain valid if `.dark` is applied later.
- Theme switching (when added) should toggle `class="dark"` on `<html>` and respect `DEFAULT_THEME = "light"`.

## Constants source of truth

Use `DEFAULT_THEME` and `SUPPORTED_THEMES` from `~/lib/constants`.
